[140.434061, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - Clamp to the target month's actual last day and derive every renewal from\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   the original anchor. Renewal dates start a new half-open cycle.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - Use actual cycle days and the old price effective at cycle start.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - Round the exact rational once using integer half-even arithmetic, independent\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   of Decimal precision.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - Preserve anchors for same-interval changes; charge the full new price and\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   re-anchor interval switches. Invoice line periods follow the respective cycles.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - Keep the existing public APIs unchanged.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ## Verification\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> Added 13 regression tests, all passing, including subprocess CLI previews for\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> all 10 finance worked examples, historical pricing, month-end/leap-day boundary\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> checks, interval switches, and exact round"]
